\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father, let me dedicate
\par All this year to Thee,
\par In whatever worldly state
\par Thou wilt have me be:
\par Not from sorrow, pain, or care,
\par Freedom dare I claim;
\par This alone shall be my prayer:
\par Glorify Thy name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Can a child presume to choose
\par Where or how to live?
\par Can a Father's love refuse
\par All the best to give?
\par More Thou givest every day
\par Than the best can claim,
\par Nor withholdest aught that may 
\par Glorify Thy name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. If in mercy Thou wilt spare
\par Joys that  yet are mine;
\par If on life, serene and fair,
\par Brighter rays may shine;
\par Let my glad heart, while it sings,
\par And whate'er the future brings,
\par Glorify Thy name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If Thou callest to the cross,
\par And its shadow come,
\par Turning all my gain to loss,
\par Shrouding heart and home;
\par Let me think how Thy dear Son
\par To His glory came,
\par And in deepest woe pray on:
\par Glorify Thy name.
\par                   Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

